## 🔧 Part 4: Common Audio Problems & Immediate Fixes

* **Problem: Microphone sounds thin, robotic, or hollow.**
  * *Root Cause:* Two active microphones competing (e.g. webcam mic + headset mic) or aggressive phase-canceling software.
  * *Fix:* Force audio input to single hardware endpoint; disable generic Windows "Microphone Boost" and manufacturer virtual surround suites.
* **Problem: Headset causes a headache or ear pressure.**
  * *Root Cause:* Excessive 4–6 kHz energy or sub-bass pressure.
  * *Fix:* Lower 5 kHz by -3 dB with Q=2.0; apply 20 Hz low-cut filter to eliminate inaudible infrasound pressure.
* **Problem: Audio crackling or popping during games.**
  * *Root Cause:* Audio buffer underrun caused by CPU core scheduling lag.
  * *Fix:* Increase PipeWire quantum buffer from 64 to 128/256 samples, or configure Real-Time Audio Priority in Linux (`rtkit`).

